{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"plugins/claude-code/hooks/hooks.json","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-09-29T14:06:52.353745Z","id":"162371d3be477aee44d5e1d2e6c1bcf26f27a43bdf9b8875642ffbced60747cc","body":{"detail":"Claude Code's SessionStart hook passes a `source` of `startup`, `resume`, `clear`, `compact`, or `fork` (per the Claude Code hooks reference: 'SessionStart hooks get a source of startup, resume, clear, compact, or fork', and the matcher-values table lists all five for SessionStart). This plugin's matcher is `\"startup|resume|clear|compact\"`, which silently excludes `fork`. A session started by forking (e.g. via a worktree or session fork) never receives the additionalContext injection -- no error, no warning, just silence, matching the hook's own documented 'Silent everywhere else' behavior for a case that was meant to fire.","kind":"blocker","span":{"start":{"line":5},"end":{"line":5},"content_hash":"18b98a2cd39d01a5355c04654de978d0ff029bbe02f33be1e6507f2cf9ce9a05"},"suggested_fix":"Add `fork` to the matcher: `\"startup|resume|clear|compact|fork\"`.","summary":"SessionStart matcher omits the `fork` source, so the hook never fires for forked sessions","tags":["review","review:claude-plugin-pr14","session:claude-code:6982e520-2dd9-4d9d-b484-c954e628c65c"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"plugins/claude-code/hooks/hooks.json","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-09-29T14:17:14.839243Z","id":"e5843ecc3a0d47ee916e94ae3781c34e6293c50c1210087d7e388fd8a8b3dc79","body":{"detail":"plugins/claude-code/hooks/hooks.json:5 is '\"matcher\": \"startup|resume|clear|compact\"'. The Claude Code hooks reference (https://code.claude.com/docs/en/hooks.md, SessionStart matcher table) lists five sources: startup, resume, clear, compact, and fork ('A new session forked from an existing one: --fork-session with --resume or --continue, the /fork background copy, or /branch'). It adds that 'Before v2.1.214, forked sessions reported source \"resume\"'. On current Claude Code, a forked or /branch session in a repository with .qual files gets no wrapper instruction and no using-qualifier context. Severity: a blocker is defensible. Forking is a common path, and without this context every skill in the plugin writes a bare `qualifier` that is not on PATH (the plugin has no bin/ directory). The fix is one word.","kind":"comment","references":"162371d3be477aee44d5e1d2e6c1bcf26f27a43bdf9b8875642ffbced60747cc","summary":"confirmed: the SessionStart matcher leaves out the documented fork source","tags":["verified","session:claude-code:6982e520-2dd9-4d9d-b484-c954e628c65c"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"plugins/claude-code/hooks/hooks.json","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-01T17:00:14.407682Z","id":"77e4c13d193ce8763f6e0c14229a023d1ba26e423941a90ed0b728e5c1187bb6","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:9b8a0136a86980787495f1656d66840fb2d6afe6","summary":"matcher is now startup|resume|clear|compact|fork (plugins/claude-code/hooks/hooks.json:5); scripts/test-plugin.sh ok: hooks.json SessionStart matcher includes startup, resume, clear, compact, fork","supersedes":"162371d3be477aee44d5e1d2e6c1bcf26f27a43bdf9b8875642ffbced60747cc","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:6982e520-2dd9-4d9d-b484-c954e628c65c"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"plugins/claude-code/hooks/session-start","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-01T20:16:51.817292Z","id":"00057ca61520a21e911e7e6c5ee20964cb21ae0567c278661da6260a7034a987","body":{"detail":"session-start:131 tells the model to run `\"<absolute plugin root>/scripts/ensure-qualifier.sh\" exec <args>`, with the path in double quotes, and calls it \"pre-approved in every qual skill\". Each SKILL.md (e.g. plugins/claude-code/skills/using-qualifier/SKILL.md:4) pre-approves `Bash(${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/scripts/ensure-qualifier.sh exec:*)`, which has no quotes. There are two gaps. (1) https://code.claude.com/docs/en/plugins-reference#where-each-variable-resolves lists where `${...}` resolves for skills as \"Anywhere in the Markdown body\". It does not mention frontmatter, so the rule may stay the literal string `${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/...` and never match. (2) Even after substitution, the rule's prefix starts with `/`, while the command the hook prints starts with `\"`. scripts/test-plugin.sh:1095-1096 only checks that the rule text is present in the frontmatter; it never checks that the rule approves the command line from session-start:131. If either gap is real, every qualifier call asks for permission, and the model is told something false.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":131},"end":{"line":131},"content_hash":"c39a34c199bd410ccc300805d91ca54f06340c104a9ca1b12e35318bfbaf0e6d"},"suggested_fix":"Load the plugin in a real session (`claude --plugin-dir ./plugins/claude-code`), invoke a qual skill, and run the exact command the hook prints. If it prompts for permission, either print the path unquoted when it contains no spaces, or make the rule and the printed form match (for example a `bin/qualifier` shim; see the allowed-tools finding on using-qualifier/SKILL.md:4). Then reword session-start:131 to say only what was observed.","summary":"The hook says the wrapper call is pre-approved in every qual skill, but nothing checks that the allowed-tools rule matches the command the hook tells the model to run","tags":["review","review:2026-10-01","session:claude-code:906ddd45-2dc1-4a64-9674-56eec33bd6f1"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"plugins/claude-code/hooks/session-start","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-01T20:18:41.780087Z","id":"6308aaeb8a29e52188dfc73619c7560330fbde8bc3acaa6f6c13f17bc4024bce","body":{"detail":"plugins/claude-code/hooks/session-start:131 prints `\"$WRAPPER\" exec <args>` (quoted path) and says it is \"pre-approved in every qual skill\". All nine plugins/claude-code/skills/*/SKILL.md:4 carry the unquoted `Bash(${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/scripts/ensure-qualifier.sh exec:*)`. scripts/test-plugin.sh:1095-1096 only asserts that the rule string is present (`assert rule in tools`). https://code.claude.com/docs/en/plugins-reference#where-each-variable-resolves lists `${...}` resolution for skill content as \"Anywhere in the Markdown body\", with no mention of frontmatter. No test or eval exercises the permission match. The finding says the failure may not happen, so concern is the right kind.","kind":"comment","references":"00057ca61520a21e911e7e6c5ee20964cb21ae0567c278661da6260a7034a987","summary":"confirmed: the pre-approval claim at session-start:131 is unverified, and the rule and the printed command differ in form","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:906ddd45-2dc1-4a64-9674-56eec33bd6f1"]}}
